# SERVED MODEL: claude-opus-5[1m]
# X.W1.b — FM-12: "untracked evidence is not evidence."
#
# The repo root ignores every PNG (`.gitignore:34` `*.png`) with one carve-out
# (`!demo/**/*.png`). Goldens ARE PNGs, so without this file a minted golden set
# is invisible to `git status`, never lands in a commit, and G-8's suite asserts
# against bytes no reviewer can see. That is the exact silent-drop shape the root
# ignore file already warns about twice in its own comments — U-F49's `/auth/`
# anchoring, and the `!test/dist/**` carve for U.W-CANON's hygiene gates.
#
# A nested negation is git's own mechanism for this, and the repo's own idiom.
# It works here because the DIRECTORY is not excluded — only `*.png` files are —
# and git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded. That is
# also why the golden directory is `goldens/` and not `__goldens__/`: a leading
# underscore would match the root `_*` rule, exclude the directory itself, and
# make re-inclusion impossible.
#
# `scripts/visual/regenerate-goldens.mjs` verifies this holds on every run and
# exits 4 if any minted golden is ignored — the rule is enforced, not trusted.

!*.png
